      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "My deepest condolences for carrying such profound frustration and injustice, especially regarding the concepts of control and inevitability. You are absolutely right that the options for a comfortable end of life can feel incredibly limited, and it is understandable that this absence of choice weighs heavily on your spirit. Please reach out to a hospice palliative care specialist who can compassionately discuss all available options, including palliative sedation or palliative care, to help you speak about how your final days should unfold. I strongly encourage you to call a therapist or counselor specifically experienced in complex grief so you can process this loss of autonomy.",
